# COMPONENT

## Experiment

### PACKAGE

org.simplemodeling.textus.experiment

### DESCRIPTION

Textus Experiment defines reproducible experiment plans and aggregates their
observations. It uses a named immutable corpus revision as common input, while
Textus AI executes profile-resolved work and application components judge
domain acceptance.

# SERVICE

## ExperimentManagement

### DESCRIPTION

Defines experiment arms, runs, and observations. An experiment can compare
multiple treatments over the same corpus revision without owning corpus content
or choosing a provider/model at an application operation boundary.

### OPERATION

#### defineExperiment

##### DESCRIPTION

Creates an experiment definition that references one immutable corpus revision
and an application acceptance operation.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
DefineExperiment

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
DefineExperimentResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-create

##### ENTITY
Experiment

#### defineExperimentArm

##### DESCRIPTION

Adds one named treatment arm. The arm references an operator-managed execution
plan rather than exposing provider, model, endpoint, or credential fields.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
DefineExperimentArm

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
DefineExperimentArmResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-create

##### ENTITY
ExperimentArm

#### activateExperiment

##### DESCRIPTION

Activates a draft experiment after at least one arm has been defined. The
corpus revision and acceptance operation become fixed for subsequent runs.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
ActivateExperiment

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
ActivateExperimentResult

#### startExperiment

##### DESCRIPTION

Starts one run against the experiment's corpus revision. Execution and domain
acceptance are connected later through normal assembled component operations.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
StartExperiment

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
StartExperimentResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-create

##### ENTITY
ExperimentRun

#### completeExperimentRun

##### DESCRIPTION

Moves a running experiment run to a terminal status and retains an optional
sanitized completion-evidence reference.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
CompleteExperimentRun

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
CompleteExperimentRunResult

#### recordObservation

##### DESCRIPTION

Records one arm result for one corpus case using redacted execution and domain
evidence references. Raw prompts, credentials, and provider payloads are not
observation fields.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
RecordObservation

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
RecordObservationResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-create

##### ENTITY
ExperimentObservation

#### listExperimentRuns

##### DESCRIPTION

Lists experiment runs for operator inspection.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
ListExperimentRuns

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
ListExperimentRunsResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-search

##### ENTITY
ExperimentRun

#### listExperimentObservations

##### DESCRIPTION

Lists recorded observations. Aggregate reports are derived from these immutable
facts rather than stored in the corpus.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
ListExperimentObservations

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
ListExperimentObservationsResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-search

##### ENTITY
ExperimentObservation

#### summarizeExperimentRun

##### DESCRIPTION

Derives deterministic outcome counts from the immutable observations retained
for one experiment run.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
SummarizeExperimentRun

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
SummarizeExperimentRunResult

# ENTITY

## Experiment

### DESCRIPTION

An experiment definition that keeps a corpus revision and application
acceptance target stable across its runs.

### Attribute

| name                       | type     | multiplicity |
|----------------------------+----------+--------------|
| id                         | entityid | 1            |
| experimentKey              | ExperimentKey | 1         |
| name                       | name     | 1            |
| corpusRevisionId           | entityid | 1            |
| acceptanceOperation        | AcceptanceOperation | 1    |
| description                | description | ?            |
| status                     | ExperimentStatus | 1       |

## ExperimentArm

### DESCRIPTION

One named treatment within an experiment. `executionPlanReference` is a
runtime-owned plan reference, not a provider or model selector.

### Attribute

| name                   | type     | multiplicity |
|------------------------+----------+--------------|
| id                     | entityid | 1            |
| experimentId           | entityid | 1            |
| armKey                 | ExperimentArmKey | 1     |
| name                   | name     | 1            |
| executionPlanReference | ExecutionPlanReference | 1 |

## ExperimentRun

### DESCRIPTION

One bounded execution of an experiment against its fixed corpus revision.

### Attribute

| name             | type     | multiplicity |
|------------------+----------+--------------|
| id               | entityid | 1            |
| experimentId     | entityid | 1            |
| corpusRevisionId | entityid | 1            |
| status           | ExperimentRunStatus | 1       |
| runReference     | ExperimentRunReference | 1    |
| completionEvidenceReference | ExperimentEvidenceReference | ? |

## ExperimentObservation

### DESCRIPTION

One arm outcome for one case. The outcome is domain-neutral; the referenced
acceptance and execution evidence retain the application-specific detail.

### Attribute

| name                        | type     | multiplicity |
|-----------------------------+----------+--------------|
| id                          | entityid | 1            |
| experimentRunId             | entityid | 1            |
| experimentArmId             | entityid | 1            |
| corpusCaseId                | entityid | 1            |
| outcome                     | ExperimentOutcome | 1      |
| acceptanceEvidenceReference | ExperimentEvidenceReference | ? |
| executionEvidenceReference  | ExperimentEvidenceReference | ? |
| metricReference             | ExperimentMetricReference | ?   |

